 "reading": "T1 does not pass the pre-registered bar on XAU/GBP (failed: confT2, conf2x, placebo). Confirmation 2016-01 → 2026-10: +0.005R a trade net (n 2089, month t +0.16; gross +0.038R, t +1.19; −0.027R at 2x costs). Discovery 2006-04 → 2015-12: +0.086R (n 1820, t +2.38; gross t +3.11). 36 of 40 placebo seeds beaten on the confirmation window (placebo median −0.016R). XAU/USD over the same windows: confirmation +0.041R (n 2049, t +1.48), discovery +0.098R (t +2.98). Monthly net-R correlation with XAU/USD T1 0.482 over 247 months; same side on 85.9 % of shared days: only partly the same trades as XAU/USD. XAU/USD itself would not clear this confirmation bar either (month t +1.48 on 2016-26 at the old $0.60 cost; the measured-cost studies are what carry it there), so the 2016-26 window is a hard test for this rule on any gold quote. Before costs XAU/GBP's confirmation is +0.038R (gross month t +1.19) against XAU/USD's +0.115R (t +4.25): the pound quote keeps about a third of the dollar quote's gross; a before-cost tilt is not an edge. Worst confirmation drawdown −116.32R. The cost is a stated 0.016 % of price, not a measured XAU/GBP spread. Nothing live changes and no proposal is written.",
 "verdict": "FAIL (confT2, conf2x, placebo): gold's T1 breakout on XAU/GBP, confirmation 2016-01 → 2026-10 +0.005R a trade net (n 2089, month t +0.16); discovery 2006-04 → 2015-12 +0.086R (n 1820, t +2.38)"
